{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/issues/5737","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/issues/5737/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/issues/5737/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/issues/5737/events","html_url":"https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/pull/5737","id":5647953376,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJ-UyCM8AAAABF6YkCQ","number":5737,"title":"feat(cake_dsa): SM107 (Rubin) generated programs and strided / packed GLM-5.2 trainer layouts for the native 64-head DSA sparse-attention training kernels (#5675)","user":{"login":"yyihuang","id":52445717,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDQ1NzE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52445717?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyihuang","html_url":"https://github.com/yyihuang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyihuang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyihuang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyihuang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyihuang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyihuang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyihuang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyihuang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyihuang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyihuang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10040634866,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJ-UyCM8AAAACVnft8g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/labels/run-ci","name":"run-ci","color":"D7BD0D","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":14,"created_at":"2026-09-30T14:20:37Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T20:46:15Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/pulls/5737","html_url":"https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/pull/5737","diff_url":"https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/pull/5737.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/pull/5737.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\nExtends the native 64-query-head DSA sparse-attention training kernels (`flashinfer.experimental.cake_dsa_train`, #5704) with:\n\n- **SM107 (Rubin R200) generated programs** for the forward and backward kernels (`csrc/cake_dsa_h64_train/sm_107a/`), regenerated\n  together with the SM100 and SM103 programs from the same source revision (one module table for the three architectures).\n- **Strided / packed trainer layouts** (GLM-5.2 style, #5675): `q_rope` taken directly from the pre-absorb `q[T,64,256]` slice\n  (channels 192:256, head stride 256), `kv` rows read in place from packed `[Tkv,576]` or `[Tkv,704]` buffers (latent `0:512` ‖\n  rope `512:576`, optional 128-channel indexer key), `dq` written into caller views, and the backward's latent+rope `dK/dV`\n  accumulated straight into a caller-provided packed fp32 `[Tkv,576]` buffer (`dkv_acc`) with an optional destination-row map\n  applied in the kernel epilogue — no `contiguous()` / `cat` / `index_add_` copies.\n- Separate `cu_seqlens_q` / `cu_seqlens_k` with an opt-in in-segment causal rule (`causal=True` on the varlen entry: a slot that\n  selects a key after the query's own position `(seqlen_k - seqlen_q) + local_q` is dropped; the default `causal=False` keeps the\n  first release's plain offsetting), `-1`-padded local key indices, empty rows (`out = 0`, `lse = -inf`, zero gradients), arbitrary\n  `T` / `Tkv` / segment lengths (no padding, no dropped tokens, no cross-segment reads).\n- Backward recomputes `P` from `lse` in 4096-token chunks (no `P` tensor), bf16 I/O, fp32 softmax statistics and fp32 `dK/dV`\n  accumulation. The existing #5704 entry points keep their signatures and default behaviour; the new options are keyword-only\n  (`causal`, `dkv_acc`, `dkv_dst_map`). `dkv_dst_map` values are the caller's invariant (the kernel does not range-check them);\n  `FLASHINFER_CAKE_DSA_CHECK_DST_MAP=1` validates them on every call.\n\n## Baselines and their source PRs / versions\n\n- **A (hard gate)**: FlashMLA sparse forward (`ba89a34`) + cuDNN frontend 1.30.0 `DSA.sparse_attention_backward_wrapper`, timed\n  with the `contiguous` / `cat` / `index_add_` glue those APIs need. FlashMLA's SM100 kernels do not run on SM107 (the CUTLASS\n  TMA/TMEM arch macros are not enabled for `__CUDA_ARCH__` 1070); on SM107 the A backward is still compared through cuDNN.\n- **B (precision / memory reference, also compared row by row)**: FlashAttention PR #2914 head `c9e2e5eb` (`flash_attn.cute` sparse\n  MLA, `recompute_p`, `token_chunk = 4096`).\n- Test oracle: chunked fp64 reference on the same bf16 inputs (`tests/experimental/test_cake_dsa_train.py`), as in #5704.\n\n## Performance\n\nTrain step = forward + backward including the layout glue each arm needs; CUPTI kernel time; median of >= 20 steps (13 at 128k),\n3 alternating rounds, every arm in its own process, bit-identical inputs, same GPU. Ratios > 1 mean this PR is faster. `peak / saved\nmem vs FA` = peak allocated / saved-activation bytes of this PR divided by FA #2914 (< 1 = less memory). No `P` tensor is kept.\n\n### SM107 (Rubin R200, 212 SMs) — final (no clock-flagged rows, all arms at 2412 MHz)\n\n| row | T | Tkv | segs | this PR fwd / bwd / step ms | FA #2914 step ms | cuDNN DSA bwd ms | FA/this step (fwd/bwd) | cuDNN bwd / this bwd | peak / saved mem vs FA |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|---|---:|---|\n| packed_glm_a | 16231 | 268757 | 8 | 2.003 / 9.554 / 11.557 | 17.197 | 12